domain SemanticSchemaCorrection:
  description "RCA and bounded local correction of recurring xAI schema rejection."
evidence E_HTTP:
  "Immutable run semantic-migration-grok-2026-09-10-v1 has one HTTP400 Unsupported response format. Self referenced definition are not supported; no completion or usage. Current generation unchanged. No new provider call is authorized."
evidence E_CODE:
  "character-semantic-change-set.ts defines operation.value as recursive z.lazy JSON union. character-migration-prompts.ts directly invokes zodResponseFormat on the shared change-set validator. Generated value definition contains array.items and object.additionalProperties references to itself; the probe forwards it unchanged."
evidence E_HISTORY:
  "Earlier character-authoring RCA identified a different producer: schemaObject parse detached the mutation target during full-definition normalization. Its fix preserves identity and its character-definition test has a private acyclic-definitions helper. That helper is not used by the migration schema or probe."
evidence E_PROCESS:
  "semantic-probe-readiness-2026-09-10.think E4/U1 treated provider schema acceptance as unknown and relied on scripted transport tests; it did not reconcile the known non-circular provider invariant with this new serializer. This is documentary evidence of a missed knowledge-transfer decision, not a claim about hidden agent thoughts."
evidence E_SPEC:
  "Official xAI structured-output documentation read 2026-09-10 permits only non-circular references. JSON Schema official basics explicitly states an empty object schema accepts any valid JSON including arbitrarily nested data. xAI rejects Boolean property schemas, so use an object schema, not true. Exact new projection acceptance by the live endpoint remains unknown."
evidence E_SCOPE:
  "ADR-0030 D6 freezes prompt and response identities per attempt. D7 retains six operations and D8-D9 retain full server validation, stateless semantic review and two repairs. Generic operation.value is not already target-specific. V3 also includes arbitrary inventory affordance.causalEnvelope but mechanical validation freezes affordance; a fixed JSON depth limit would add an unsupported constraint. Existing v1 probe artifacts and pending receipts are historical evidence, not a retry authority."
premise ALTERNATIVES:
  "Recursive internal typing is valid; defect is using its executable validator representation as a provider grammar without a provider projection. Earlier alias-copy defect, content semantics and token exhaustion do not explain this submitted true recursive graph. A missing test explains escape, not schema production. A finite target-specific grammar adds complexity; arbitrary depth or string encoding would change values or contract; disabling strict output weakens the envelope."
decision ROOT based_on E_HTTP, E_CODE, E_HISTORY, E_PROCESS, ALTERNATIVES:
  "C-SCHEMA-001 high confidence defect-producing cause: conflation of application JSON validation and provider output grammar at CHANGE_SCHEMA generation. Contributing mechanism: separate provider paths allowed the known invariant to remain feature-local. C-SCHEMA-002 high confidence process decision failure: readiness reused local test success without reconciling the known provider invariant; exact private mental cause unknown. Escape cause: scripted transport and authoring-only regression did not examine the new outgoing schema. HTTP400 is the trigger/detection, not a new unknown provider limitation."
decision CORRECTION based_on ROOT, E_SPEC, E_SCOPE, ALTERNATIVES:
  "Implement a versioned provider projection that substitutes only the exact generated generic-JSON definition with the standard any-JSON object schema, retaining strict envelope, required value, all other definitions, direct typed values and unchanged authoritative receive/merge/semantic validators. Assert the expected generic definition shape before substitution; never erase an arbitrary cycle. No depth cap, string encoding, field loss or six-operation change. Preserve v1 payload construction for historical replay; v2 prompt selects corrected grammar and tests use v2. Keep consumed v1 probe fixture and evidence untouched."
decision PREVENTION based_on ROOT, CORRECTION, E_HISTORY:
  "Reuse the acyclic-reference invariant as a shared xAI outgoing-schema check at the two strict-output boundaries before network/retry/provider accounting, covering definitions, defs, root and escaped local pointers. Do not forbid recursion for other providers. Regression tests must reproduce the retained failed request, reject direct/transitive cycles before fetch, and prove corrected grammar preserves required fields and unbounded typed JSON. Inspect other outgoing paths: current stream/tools use json_object and have no submitted strict schema. Do not widen into unrelated stream/tool redesign."
decision ACTION based_on CORRECTION, PREVENTION, E_SCOPE:
  "User authorized correction and uncompromising RCA. Implement and test locally, record causal chain and remaining live-provider uncertainty, inspect Seal impact and preserve historical probe evidence. No production writes, provider calls, retry, activation, commit, push, global guidance edits or new accepted architecture. Verify local source correction separately from detection improvement. Do not report production or real-LLM resolution."

evidence E_COVERAGE:
  "Read-only search across backend/src found an additional strict-output client in scripts/evaluate-perception-prompts.ts at completeJson, passing input.responseFormat directly. Other discovered scripts use json_object. Earlier two-boundary coverage was limited to llm/ and must not be presented as repository-wide."
evidence E_TYPECHECK:
  "Full tests passed 765 tests, but tsc reports two TS2345 errors in new provider-response-schema.test.ts: required ProviderConfig.modelFast is omitted in both fixtures. Production constructor has a runtime modelFast fallback, but ProviderConfig still requires the property. No runtime source defect is inferred from this fixture construction error."
decision FOLLOWUP based_on E_COVERAGE, E_TYPECHECK, PREVENTION:
  "Use the same xAI-only guard in the discovered evaluation entry before its request; inspect existing three perception formats and every character authoring format in regression tests. This is the same provider invariant, not a different product feature. Fix the two test configuration producers by supplying explicit modelFast; do not weaken ProviderConfig or cast the fixtures. The typecheck caught a test-only construction mistake, not the original schema root cause. Then rerun validation."

evidence E_TARGET:
  "Read-only generation of CharacterDefinitionV3Schema for prompt targetDefinitionSchema reveals five direct self-referencing aliases (reach, requiresSight, mobility, requiresSpeech, requiresUsableHeldObject), each with its default. Concrete enum/boolean definitions exist at basicAction.mechanics.constraints.properties. Existing V2 authoring normalizer repairs these aliases only inside its private characterDefinitionResponseFormat. This target schema is prompt input, not submitted response_format."
decision TARGET_CAUSE based_on E_TARGET, E_HISTORY, E_CODE:
  "C-SCHEMA-003 high confidence: new migration target-schema generation bypasses the existing domain-specific alias normalization and supplies unresolved aliases as target guidance. This is a second manifestation of feature-local projection handling, not proof of any model semantic error: the real run failed before generation. Do not identify prompt aliases as the HTTP400 cause; the submitted change-set grammar has its separate true-recursion fault."
decision TARGET_CORRECTION based_on TARGET_CAUSE, CORRECTION:
  "Extract and reuse one character-definition alias normalizer for both V2 authoring output and v2 migration V3 target guidance, using exact generated definition names and concrete typed constraint properties. Preserve the known identity fix, defaults and all non-alias content. Keep old migration prompt v1 target guidance byte-identical for replay. Test the five replacements, rejection of unrelated cycles and unchanged input. This is contract-preserving projection repair within accepted V2/V3 semantics, not a new character behavior or an ADR rewrite."

evidence E_NARROW:
  "tsc rejected new character-definition-response-schema.ts line8 with TS2322: the inline non-null object/array exclusion narrows unknown only to object, not Record<string, unknown>. Runtime shape checks exist, but TypeScript has no declared checked record predicate there."
decision NARROW based_on E_NARROW, TARGET_CORRECTION:
  "Use an explicit type predicate whose runtime checks establish a non-null non-array record, matching the existing shared graph checker. Do not use a type assertion, string round-trip, or change returned identity. This fixes the new compile-time helper mismatch; it is separate from the incident root cause."
